Accounted resident recovery regression integration — 2026-11-24
================================================================

Scope
-----
Eight causal regressions cover interrupted generation, a remaining Message/Finish
suffix, a singleton Finish with fresh human approval or rejection and no new
draws, old pending-case labels, evaluator candidate exhaustion across handoffs,
independent rollback/window/revision requirements, Stop at preopen/per-event/
Ready, closed option grammar, and canonical future input/endpoint custody.

Integration base: b6fba84ce63bf2fbe4170ded8682b1cb43412104.
A concurrent main update supplied resident recovery production changes while
this work was in progress. Those production changes and their tests are
preserved. This change adds the independently authored causal regression module
and its bounded evaluator-child mode to that current implementation.

Source review
-------------
A second reviewer reviewed the production paths and test designs. Review found
and corrected a singleton-Finish fixture that had published only the first of
two Messages. The final fixture publishes both Messages, retires each completed
helper cohort through the production retirement method under a finite cleanup
bound, and resumes after Message 2 at position 6 with four sampled draws. Finish
must retain that original spend; only two final applied reviews advance the
evaluation revision.

